   32.0   32.0  368.9 "Dave Winer · 5 March 2024 · Scripting News"
   77.0   32.0  638.7 "People learn to make art by studying previous artists. Would we want it any"
  106.0   32.0   94.7 "other way?"
  151.0   32.0  583.6 "Imagine if everyone had to reinvent everything that anyone had ever"
  180.0   32.0  323.6 "invented just to make something new."
  225.0   32.0  621.6 "There is a lot of that in software, people won't put in an API so you have to"
  254.0   32.0  383.0 "rebuild the whole house just to get a window."
  299.0   32.0  564.8 "We can make progress when people don't try to lock up their ideas."
  344.0   32.0  642.8 "Individuals live just a short time, we can't do that much in a lifetime, but we"
  373.0   32.0  653.1 "are an amazing species, because we leave behind what we learn and we build."
  418.0   32.0  324.5 "[image: We learn by studying ourselves.]"
  463.0   32.0  611.0 "So why shouldn't our machines be able to learn too? They already can do"
  492.0   32.0  590.8 "things vastly more complex than we can. We've invented a huge lever."
  537.0   32.0  591.9 "Science fiction tells us that we will lose control and be enslaved by our"
  566.0   32.0  632.2 "machines. I love those stories, like the Matrix and Battlestar Galactica. But"
  595.0   32.0  607.8 "those are stories, they didn't happen. The future is rarely so predictable."
  624.0   32.0  317.2 "Things interact in unforseeable ways."
  669.0   32.0  610.8 "We're at dead-ends in climate and government. We need to make radical"
  698.0   32.0  639.6 "changes, and a fresh invention as radically progressive as any that has come"
  727.0   32.0  231.6 "before is now in our hands."
  772.0   32.0  236.2 "[image: We're going to use it.]"
  817.0   32.0  402.6 "PS: I wrote the words, ChatGPT did the images."
